\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 \strokec2 Why no v4\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 A v4 would have to be either (a) a "v2 with five paragraph improvements" \'97 which is just edits to v2, or (b) a maximalist that adds new counts \'97 but the May 2026 work doesn't unlock new counts beyond what v3 already pleads. Creating a v4 would fragment the maintenance burden across four versions instead of three and would add no strategic capability that the in-place updates don't already provide.\
The four updated files now form a coherent set: the Overview maps every argument to a draft, each draft pleads the arguments at the appropriate level of detail, and the Research notes blocks (which counsel removes before filing) cite the underlying strength assessment and motion-tactics files for the reasoning behind each rating.\
